Rule 1 (Input tensor must have dimension 1 or 2)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) = 1) ∨ (ndim(v_1) = 2)
>>
Rule 6 (Example: if v_1's element type is int, then v_2 cannot be negative.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 2 then v_2 ≥ 0
>>
Rule 12 (Input tensor cannot be boolean type)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 0
>>
Rule 24 (Data type of input tensor should be numerical)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_1) ≠ 0) ∧ (dtype_(v_1) ≠ 11)
>>
Rule 30 (Input should be a tensor of numerical or boolean values)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_1) = 0) ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = 1) ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = 2) ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = 3) ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = 4) ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = 5) ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = 6) ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = 7) ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = 8) ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = 9) ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = 10)
>>
Rule 36 (The dimension of input tensor cannot be greater than 2)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≤ 2
>>
Rule 48 (If the tensor is complex, k has to be zero.)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: int} |= if (dtype_(v_1) = 9) ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = 10) then v_2 = 0
